    "number": 36668,
    "state": "open",
    "state_reason": null,
    "title": "util: Make files opened via `fsbridge::fopen()` not inheritable by child processes",
    "body": "Files opened via [`fsbridge::fopen()`](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/blob/dd9d2b919d6a97907417bf9c4f539f182f04cc01/src/util/fs.cpp#L23-L30) are inherited by child processes, such as `-*notify` or `-signer` commands.\n\nThey should not be, as a child has no business with the node's open files. On POSIX systems this can be achieved with `O_CLOEXEC`. On Windows, with the `N` mode flag (`_O_NOINHERIT`).\n\nOn Windows, this manifests as a functional test that passes all its cases and then fails to clean up:\n```\nPermissionError: [WinError 32] The process cannot access the file because it is being used by another process: ‘D:\\a\\temp\\test_runner₿🏃20261026_100424\\feature_versionbits_warning_0\\node0\\regtest\\debug.log’\n```\n\nPreviously reported in #28529 and #27352.",
    "user": {
